# Frame With Me — always apply

Read and obey `.specify/memory/constitution.md` for every change.

## Priorities
1. Security & user data safety  
2. Memory efficiency / no leaks  
3. On-demand loading & perceived speed  
4. Separation of concerns (UI → use-cases → repositories → adapters)  
5. Reusable design-system UI + en/te/hi i18n  
6. Tests for domain logic  

## Hard rules
- Admin controls = **web app only**, not Android
- Notifications/payments only via **ports/adapters**
- No hardcoded user-facing strings; use `t()` / i18n keys
- Paginate lists; never fetch all rows for UI
- After every code change: complete `.specify/checklists/post-change-security-memory.md` and report PASS/FAIL in the reply
- User-facing work: run Customer Perspective Agent (`.cursor/agents/customer-perspective.md`)

## Spec Kit
Active feature: `.specify/feature.json` → `specs/001-mvp-android/`  
Prefer updating `spec.md` / `plan.md` / `tasks.md` when behavior changes.
